There's no existing project in the current directory. Since you mentioned you have an existing project, here's exactly what to add:

**1. Create `Middleware/ApiExceptionHandler.cs`:**

```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Diagnostics;
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc;

namespace YourApp.Middleware;

internal sealed class ApiExceptionHandler(ILogger<ApiExceptionHandler> logger)
    : IExceptionHandler
{
    public async ValueTask<bool> TryHandleAsync(
        HttpContext httpContext,
        Exception exception,
        CancellationToken cancellationToken)
    {
        var (statusCode, title) = exception switch
        {
            KeyNotFoundException => (StatusCodes.Status404NotFound, "Not Found"),
            ArgumentException => (StatusCodes.Status400BadRequest, "Bad Request"),
            InvalidOperationException => (StatusCodes.Status409Conflict, "Conflict"),
            _ => (0, (string?)null)
        };

        if (statusCode == 0)
            return false; // Default handler returns 500 with no sensitive details

        logger.LogWarning(exception, "Handled API exception: {Title}", title);

        httpContext.Response.StatusCode = statusCode;
        await httpContext.Response.WriteAsJsonAsync(new ProblemDetails
        {
            Status = statusCode,
            Title = title,
            Detail = title,
            Instance = httpContext.Request.Path
        }, cancellationToken);

        return true;
    }
}
```

**2. In `Program.cs`, register the services and middleware:**

```csharp
// Services (before builder.Build())
builder.Services.AddExceptionHandler<ApiExceptionHandler>();
builder.Services.AddProblemDetails();

// Middleware (after builder.Build(), before app.MapXxx())
app.UseExceptionHandler();
app.UseStatusCodePages();
```

**How it works:**

- `IExceptionHandler` intercepts exceptions globally — no per-endpoint try-catch needed
- Known exceptions map to appropriate status codes with safe messages
- Unknown exceptions fall through (`return false`), and the default `UseExceptionHandler` + `AddProblemDetails()` combo returns a 500 Problem Details response with no exception details leaked
- `UseStatusCodePages` ensures non-exception error codes (e.g., 404 from routing) also get Problem Details formatting

All responses will have `Content-Type: application/problem+json` per RFC 7807.
